.TH STRIP 1 "March 15, 1972" "UNIX Fourth Edition" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
v4-strip \- remove symbols and relocation bits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B strip
.I name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I strip
removes the symbol table and relocation bits ordinarily attached to the output
of the assembler and loader.
This is useful for saving space after a program has been debugged.
.PP
The effect of
.I strip
is the same as using the \fB\-s\fR option of
.I ld.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /tmp/stm?
temporary file
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBv4-ld\fR(1), \fBv4-as\fR(1)
.SH BUGS
